# Executable API walkthrough for the VS Code REST Client extension
# (humao.rest-client) and JetBrains HTTP Client. Run requests top to
# bottom: each # @name makes the response referencable, so tokens and
# ids flow into the next request automatically.
#
# Prerequisites: `make up-app` (or `make up` + `make run`).
# Full endpoint reference: docs/API.md.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Liveness: always 200 while the process runs
# @name healthz
GET {{host}}/healthz

### Readiness: 200 when postgres answers, 503 during shutdown
# @name readyz
GET {{host}}/readyz

### Register Alice
# Repeated runs answer 409 {"slug":"email-taken"} — that is expected.
# @name registerAlice
POST {{host}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "demo-pass-123",
  "displayName": "Alice"
}

### Login Alice
# @name loginAlice
POST {{host}}/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "demo-pass-123"
}

###
@token = {{loginAlice.response.body.token}}

### Create a lot (Alice is the owner)
# @name createLot
POST {{host}}/api/lots
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Antique blacksmith hammer",
  "description": "Hand-forged head, oak handle.",
  "startPriceMinor": 5000,
  "currency": "USD",
  "endsAt": "2027-01-01T12:00:00Z"
}

###
@lotID = {{createLot.response.body.id}}

### Browse active lots (public, supports ?page=, ?pageSize=, ?q=)
# @name listLots
GET {{host}}/api/lots?q=hammer

### One lot by id (public)
# @name getLot
GET {{host}}/api/lots/{{lotID}}

### Register Bob — the bidder
# @name registerBob
POST {{host}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bob@example.com",
  "password": "demo-pass-123",
  "displayName": "Bob"
}

### Login Bob
# @name loginBob
POST {{host}}/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bob@example.com",
  "password": "demo-pass-123"
}

###
@token2 = {{loginBob.response.body.token}}

### Bob bids on Alice's lot
# Must beat currentPriceMinor, otherwise 409 {"slug":"bid-too-low"}.
# Alice bidding on her own lot would get 403 {"slug":"owner-cannot-bid"}.
# @name placeBid
POST {{host}}/api/lots/{{lotID}}/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{token2}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amountMinor": 6000
}

### Bid history, newest first (public)
# @name bidHistory
GET {{host}}/api/lots/{{lotID}}/bids

### Who am I (Bob's profile)
# @name me
GET {{host}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token2}}

### Edit the lot (owner only, PATCH semantics: omitted fields stay)
# After placeBid above this answers 409 {"slug":"lot-has-bids"}: a lot
# with bids is frozen — that is the business rule, not a bug.
# @name updateLot
PATCH {{host}}/api/lots/{{lotID}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Hand-forged head, oak handle. Pickup only."
}
